        "notes": "Inspiration: Revvy's Belgian Blonde https://www.homebrewtalk.com/threads/revvys-belgian-blonde-leffe-clone.202852/\n\nTargets based on Belgian Leffe Blonde product data: OG 1.063 (15.5 °P), FG 1.013-1.014, 6.6% ABV, 21.5 IBU and 13 EBC. If brewhouse efficiency is higher than the repository's 48% planning assumption, dilute to the target OG before pitching.\n\nFourth iteration adds maize to reflect the commercial ingredient list and increases simple sugar for a drier finish. Retains T-58 for its spicy, clove-like fermentation character, but lowers the mash from 70°C to 65°C to address v3's high 1.020 FG. No spices are added: BJCP describes them as non-traditional, while Leffe's published ingredient list attributes the character to malt, maize, sugar and hops. Target about 3.0 volumes of CO₂ when packaging.",
